Avengers in game took secrecy to all new  levels with its intentionally spoiler  free marketing efforts once the movie  was released though the behind the  scenes info began pouring out here are  some of the most interesting things to  emerge it's a well-known fact that  directors Joe and Anthony Russo will go  to extreme lengths to keep their marvel  creations under wraps for example they  teasingly apologized to the spoiler  prone Tom Holland for dusting Spidey at  the end of infinity war and consequently  keeping him at arm's length for the  promotion of endgame  they also pretended to fire Mark Ruffalo  after a string of spoilers had put him  on thin ice one of the best methods for  keeping everyone in the dark though was  the way the Russos handled the script  most of the actors got only pieces of  the screenplay to work from and  apparently Ruffalo got a particularly  spoiler proof of the script the hulk  actor was only given a partial script  with additional dummy scenes in it  according to an interview with E news I  don't know what's gonna happen  I like shot five different endings I  didn't even get a whole script but even  that didn't stop him from accidentally  giving something away in that same  interview he joked about what he  presumably thought was one of those  dummy scenes his spoiler they have to  throw mark off the scent oops  endgame is the second MCU outing for  Carol Danvers who arrived on the scene  just weeks earlier in her own superhero  flick Captain Marvel for actress brie  Larson though that wasn't the case  Larson had filmed her scenes for endgame  before she ever had a chance to flesh  out the character in her own film as an  added twist the first scene she ever  filmed was set during the events of  endgame but technically ended up in  Captain Marvel on The Tonight Show  Larson recalled that her first day of  filming was for the end credits scene  for her own film which showed her  arriving at the Avengers facility post  snap where's fury I didn't know that was  a tag for Captain Marvel I didn't know  what that was that we were shooting was  also nobody else there in true Russo  fashion though the actress was only  given her lines and filmed her part  alone in front of a green screen that's  taking secrecy to a whole new level  while the Russo brothers bent over  backwards to keep actors like Ruffalo  Holland and Larson from spoiling the  script there was  person that they didn't mind showing the  whole thing to Robert Downey jr. while  discussing infinity war and in game in  an interview with Rotten Tomatoes the  pair talked about keeping things secret  our DJ was probably the only one to  actually read the entire script part of  our motivation to do that is it just  takes a lot of pressure off of people  everything had started with Iron Man  just a decade earlier with end game  ultimately serving as the iron Avengers  swan song it's only appropriate that our  DJ would be trusted with some of the  most sensitive MCU knowledge to ever  exist when the Avengers break into teams  for their time heist in in-game rocket  and four are sent to Asgard during the  events of Thor the dark world to  retrieve the reality stone at that point  in time the stone is using the god of  thunders X Jane Foster as a host foster  who's been absent for Marvel films since  the dark world appears on screen a few  times before rocket is able to get the  reality stone out of her but it turns  out that foster actress Natalie Portman  didn't actually film any new footage for  endgame in an interview with  Entertainment Weekly the Russos  explained that they had been able to  salvage unused footage from the dark  world in order to get all of the scenes  they needed while the footage was enough  for them to work with they did ask the  actress to record a small bit of  voice-over in the days after endgame lit  up the theater marquees star-lord actor  Chris Pratt stirred up attention by  releasing a video he'd taken on set  while preparing for one of the film's  key action sequences the once in a  lifetime video showed nearly all of the  famous actors mostly in sweats and  comfortable clothing chatting and  discussing their scenes as casually as  if they were a group of high schoolers  hanging out after class the video gave a  unique glimpse into the inner workings  of a film that had been kept tightly  under wraps since day one  Stan Lee was a comic book Titan for over  half a century while he was an important  creative mind behind the scenes for  decades his long relationship with  Marvel also led to a memorable series of  fan favorite cameos throughout various  Marvel movies when Lee passed away in  late 2018 fans began theorizing about  when his last cameo would surface a year  earlier it had been revealed that Lee  had filmed five different cameos for  upcoming films the fact that he was  apparently batching his cameos naturally  left the possibility that he could be  popping into films for an indefinite  amount of  I'm endgame delivered a shot of a  younger looking hippie version of me  driving by the 1970s shield headquarters  shouting make love not war as it turned  out that scene will be Lee's last ever  cameo and it's a fitting farewell the  Russos confirmed after the fact that  it's the last Stan Lee cameo that made  it to film in a twist that few people  saw coming in in game Natasha Romanov  ended up sacrificing herself for the  soulstone it was a beautifully  redemptive way to end her own heroic  story which had been going on in the  background for nearly the entire MCU but  of course this is Marvel and there's  always the question of whether they'll  bring her back with Gamora zari entrance  into the future from the past in endgame  anything is possible  except not with Romanoff her story seems  closed for good this time  screenwriters Christopher Markus and  Stephen McFeely explained to the New  York Times her journey and our minds had  come to an end if she could get the  Avengers back she has a chance to get  them back that's the thing she would  trade for during her memorial scene on  the dock the surviving heroes  conversation drove home the point that  the cost of the soul stone is a  permanent one while there's no doubt  that Black Widow will be remembered by  fans for years to come she's gone for  good  except presumably for her upcoming movie  while Black Widow may have ultimately  been given a powerful closing to her own  story Romanovs death wasn't always a  sure thing after all movies aren't  completely finished until the release  date the shwarma end credits scene from  Avengers wasn't even added until the  week that the film was released so it  should come as no surprise that there  was a lot of shifting and changing as  they went along one of those changes the  events on Boromir writers Markus and  McFeely explained that there was a  version of the script that had Clint  Barton sacrificing himself for the stone  instead of Romanov but when they gave  the scene to the visual effects producer  Jim underdahl she apparently told them  don't you take this away from her the  response clearly impacted the writers  who ultimately acknowledged that it had  to be Romanoff it turns out the Markus  and McFeely have had a working master  document since Captain America Civil War  where they kept track of different  things they wanted to do with their  hero's character arcs it turns out that  endgame was the movie where they got to  run wild in particular McFeely said that  they wanted to explore Marvel's Trudeau  what if comics alternate-universe  presentations of Marvel events playing  out differently  the writers delve in and incorporated a  bunch of what-if scenarios right into  the in-game plot the writers told the  New York Times well this is our what if  if you lost four becomes fat natasha  becomes a shut-in steve becomes  depressed tony gets on with his life  Hulk is a superhero Clint becomes a  murdering maniac  while there were solid reasons for every  characters shift in tone there's no  doubt that the writers were happy to  push the heroes out of their comfort  zone for the entertainment of all  infinity war and in game maybe two  distinctly different movies but the  subject matter that they handle is  clearly interwoven this left the writers  and directors constantly scrambling to  figure out how to puzzle a bunch of  different pieces of storyline together  in a coherent way that left them with  two distinct yet connected movies at one  point the plan was to have Hulk and  banner resolve their differences in  infinity war however it felt like too  much of a positive in the middle of a  pretty sad ending so the filmmakers  bumped into endgame they also left out  the actual transformation banking on  Scott Lang in the dinner scene to  provide the right amount of confusion to  help bridge the gap in the same vein  Hawk eyes opening scene in endgame where  he loses his family was nearly tacked  onto the end of infinity war but it once  again felt out of place the biggest  decision of all was where to place the  snap they debated putting it earlier an  infinity war but it would have left  almost nothing for the ending on the  other hand if they pushed it to endgame  it would have left the first movie with  no ending at all knowing when to reverse  the snap was nearly as challenging  thankfully the creative minds behind the  scenes managed to eventually pull it all  together into two coherent stories Scott  Lang was right in-game is a time heist  movie it wasn't the writers who came up  with that one though but Marvel boss  Kevin Feige himself psyches original  suggestion was to use time travel to  resolve an infinity war plot with the  centerpiece being the time stone it  wasn't until the filmmakers began  fleshing things out that the quantum  realm became the key plot device to move  the time travel element forward once  time travel was in the mix there was one  obvious point that had to make it into  the film the Battle of New York but the  writers initially felt it was too  pandering  to head back to the original Avengers  film so they tried a ton of alternatives  first at one point they had Tony Stark  on Asgard in a stealth suit fighting  Heimdall and the planet Morag was  originally underwater at another point  the Avengers stopped by Triskelion and  even hopped in a car to visit dr.  strange when the rubber hit the road  though writers and directors alike  finally decided that heading back to the  Chitauri infested streets of New York  was the best option of the bunch  the sequence in end game when our heroes  put their heist plan to the test shows  the time travel within the MCU is  distinctly different than the way it's  been represented in movies like Timecop  Hot Tub Time Machine or Back to the  Future  Time Machine it also establishes that  Pym particles are in extremely limited  supply Tony Stark and Steve Rogers head  back on a potentially one-way trip to  the 70s in the hope of scrounging up  more particles just to keep everything  from falling apart this left fans  scratching their heads when nebula  casually brought Thanos his entire  planet size ship in its massive army  into the present where on earth did they  get the impossibly huge number of  particles to pull off a stuff like that  Joe Russo cleared up to disconnect in an  interview offering an elegantly simple  solution when 2014 nebula surrenders the  Pym particles to her father they aren't  for him to use to time-travel they're  for scientific research  Thanos a genius himself with the help of  the powerful sorcerer ebony maw studied  the Pym particles and then mass-produced  them in order to defeat the avengers  once and for all check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about the Avengers are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one
 

